
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I&#8217;ve been dipping my toe in the interview process after a year+ on the <a href="https://randsinrepose.com/archives/the-one-about-the-pro-leisure-circuit/">Pro Leisure Circuit</a>. One of the more recent interviews was with a hardware company out of LA. When we first started chatting, I explained, &#8220;I&#8217;m a consumer software guy who has been hardware adjacent.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Their response: &#8220;Don&#8217;t worry, we have plans; you&#8217;d be a great fit.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Interviews. Then more interviews. I&#8217;m intrigued, but not sold.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The robots are excellent at research, so I researched. Interviews, podcasts, press releases, LinkedIn profiles. They wouldn&#8217;t tell me why I was a great fit, so I&#8217;d use the robots to figure it out. Several hours later, I jokingly realized why they wanted me. I typed this realization into Claude not because I was expecting a response, but&#8230; because.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;They want me to build <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skynet_%28Terminator%29">Skynet</a>.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">To which Claude immediately responded, &#8220;At least when it achieves consciousness, you&#8217;ll have equity.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">R.I.P. that opportunity.</p>
